		(uuid "bc0023fb-2d0c-4b40-9a38-3d96125f8a17")
	)
	(text "2026, Christian Tambe. Some rights reserved."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.59 302.006 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bc62f120-8a32-4506-ae19-de67cbf2f001")
	)
	(text_box "Digilent 12-pin Pmod (JA).  Pins 1-4 and 7-10 are signals through 200R series resistors; \npins 5/11 are GND and 6/12 are VCC3V3 -- so a 2x6 header carries EIGHT signals, not twelve, \nwhich is why the names skip JA5/JA6.  No decoupling here: the Pmod spec puts bypassing on the \nmodule, and VCC3V3 already carries ~\n70uF.  The Cmod A7 has none at its Pmod either. \nJA1-JA4 (the top row, the half a Pmod uses for SPI) are all in bank 16: A14 A15 B15 A16. \nJA7 is C15, also bank 16.  JA8/JA9/JA10 are W19/N2/W7 -- banks 14/35/34 -- because nothing \nelse was free.  All five banks are VCCO=3.3V, so this costs timing coherence, not levels."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 161.385 247.142 0)
		(size -128.365 14.224)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0ed571f9-d293-4fcc-886a-5c70ac85048c")
	)
	(text_box "X2: 40 pins on a 2.54 mm grid, rows 22.86 mm (0.900 in) apart, numbered 1-40 straight \nthrough from the right and skipping both landings.  The two rows are mirror images. \nTOP ROW, x 59.69 down to 1.27: GND (pin 1), CHAN-CLK (2), CHAN0..CHAN6 (3-9), \n  then CHAN7..CHAN13 (10-16), GND, +3.3V, +1.8V, +1.0V (17-20). \nBOTTOM ROW, x 59.69 down to 1.27: GND, VU, RST# (pins 21-23), CHAN14..CHAN16 (24-26), \n  CHAN17..CHAN19 (27-29), then CHAN20..CHAN28 (30-38), ANALOG-IO0, ANALOG-IO1 (39, 40). \nFOUR positions in each row -- x 36.83, 34.29, 31.75, 29.21, between pins 9 and 10 above \n  and between pins 29 and 30 below -- are RESERVED, not spare: the edge-mounted \n  micro-USB X1 lands on the top row (7.80 mm of copper), the top-side LiPo header X4 \n  (JST B2B-PH-SM4-TB, 7.95 mm body) lands on the bottom row directly opposite it. \n  Each landing is 12.70 mm between the neighbouring pin centres, 11.176 mm clear. \nTHREE grounds: pins 1, 17, 21.  Pin 18 is the only +3.3V pin.  Pin 22 VU SOURCES the \n  4.4 V rail (bq24232 OUT) -- the +5V-INPUT pin and its D2/D3 went on 2026-09-09, \n  so external power is the LiPo on X4.  THE PCB FOOTPRINT MUST BE REDRAWN: 40 pads named 1-40."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 132.298 18.796 0)
